<!--
Components register — schema reference.
Copy to architecture/components/[component-name].md and fill in.
Files ending in .example are ignored by the records-query skill.

The records-query skill reads the `# ` title as `name` and each `## ` section as a
field: Used Technology -> technology, Specific Requirements -> requirements.
A section whose lines are all `- ` bullets is returned as a list; otherwise as text.
Keep the section names below unchanged so queries stay consistent across components.
-->

# component-name

## Description

What this component is responsible for, in two or three sentences. Stick to
responsibility and boundaries — implementation detail belongs in the code.

## Type

Service | Library | Datastore | Worker | Gateway | External system

## Used Technology

- Language and runtime, with major version
- Framework
- Datastore or broker it embeds

## Dependencies

- other-component
- external-system

## Specific Requirements

Operational and security requirements that constrain this component: availability
expectations, rate limiting, data retention, secrets handling, PII classification.
Reference the ADR that established each one.
